# Test sources are not needed to build a binary.
**/*_test.go

# Local build output and workspaces.
build/_workspace
build/_bin
build/bin

# Consensus fixture submodules. Several gigabytes, read only by the test
# suites, and never by a build.
tests/testdata
tests/testdata-etc
tests/evm-benchmarks

# Not part of any build.
.github
docs

# Working notes, which are not tracked and have no business entering a build
# context or an intermediate layer.
.local

# .git is deliberately NOT excluded. internal/build/env.go reads the commit,
# its date and any tag pointing at HEAD from it, guarding each read on the
# directory existing -- so excluding it does not fail the build, it silently
# produces a binary that reports no commit. For a consensus client that
# traceability is worth the build context it costs.
